# {{ .Name | title }}

A type-safe API built with [EchoNext](https://github.com/abdussamadbello/echonext).

## Features

- 🚀 Type-safe HTTP handlers
- 📝 Automatic OpenAPI generation
- 🔧 Request/response validation
- 🗄️ Database integration with GORM
- 🔄 Schema migrations with [Atlas](https://atlasgo.io)
- 🐳 Docker support
- 🧪 Comprehensive testing

## Quick Start

### Prerequisites

- Go 1.21+
- PostgreSQL
- [Atlas CLI](https://atlasgo.io/getting-started/) (for migrations)

Install Atlas:
```bash
# macOS
brew install ariga/tap/atlas

# Linux
curl -sSf https://atlasgo.sh | sh
```

### Development

```bash
# Install dependencies
go mod tidy

# Set database URL
export DATABASE_URL='postgres://postgres:password@localhost:5432/{{ .Name }}_dev?sslmode=disable'

# Start development database
make dev-db

# Run migrations
make db-migrate

# Start API server
make run-api

# Start background worker (in separate terminal)
make run-worker

# Run tests
make test
```

### API Documentation

Visit http://localhost:8080/api/docs for interactive API documentation.

### Build & Deploy

```bash
# Build all executables
make build

# Build Docker images
make docker-build

# Deploy with Docker Compose
make docker-up

# Or run directly from infrastructure folder
cd infrastructure && docker-compose up -d
```

